  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for Public Administration (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 15+16+15+16+15+14+15+15 = 121 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 121). The degree type is not printed on the plan; BA is used as the program is a public-affairs/social-science program (verify via aic.edu if strict confirmation is needed). PSY2820/PSY2821 Advanced Statistics with Lab is 4 credits. Senior capstone: PAM4000 Public Administration Capstone (printed as PAM4000 on the plan; the List of Requirements shows PAM4800 — transcribed as PAM4000 per the semester plan). Internship: PAM4899 Internship in Public Administration or a general elective (one slot in Senior Fall, one in Senior Spring; students take the internship once). Communication requirement (Junior Fall): choose COM1281 Introduction to Mass Communication, COM2630 Writing for Media, ENG2213 Public Speaking, or ENG2280 Professional and Technical Writing. Philosophy requirement (Sophomore Fall): PHI1000 Introduction to Critical Thinking or PHI1200 Introduction to Philosophy. Major requirements: ACC1201, ACC2210, ECO1401, ECO1402, MGT1400, MGT2400, MGT3201, MGT3202, MGT3213, POL1400, PSY2302, PSY2820/2821, SOC1100, SOC2420, SOC2631, PAM1000, PAM2000, PAM3000, PAM4000, PAM4899. General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab; PSY2302 counts as math), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
